It was demolished.

418
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Tüne ye.
 
It doesn't exist.

419
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Xerabî, heta sevî şeşê bî, û beri vê jî siliya bî.
 
It was ruined, it was up to grade six, and before that it
was middle school [level].

420
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Ê yanî ê kevin, beri vê çêr solî dixwandin.
 
Meaning the old ones, before this they studied for forty
years.

421
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Diçûn Kurê dixwandin.
 
They used to go to Kurê to study.

422
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Kurê?
 
Kurê?

423
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Xulu ew gundê hamber me kî der e?
 
Uncle, what place is that village opposite us?

424
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Hewa Kurê ye.
 
That is Kurê.

425
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Hew Kurê ye?
 
Is that Kurê?

426
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Jêrî gundê şêxî...
 
That is Kurê.

427
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Jêrî gundê şêxî...
 
Below the Sheikh's village...

428
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Tan malbat ne Kurê?
 
How many families [clans] are in Kurê?

429
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,000
Mesxerî kêv bikile aceb.
 
I wonder if I should make a joke.

430
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Erê mesxeriyo bike, lat mesxeriyo hez dike.
 
Yes, make the joke, the people like jokes.

431
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Na na.
 
No, no.

432
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Berê digotin, o... mal nehe, axa dehe.
 
Before they used to say, oh... nine houses, ten Aghas
[Lords].

433
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Mal nehe, axa dehe?
 
Nine houses, ten Aghas?

434
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Heye, teqîben sî mal heye.
 
There are, approximately thirty houses.

435
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Wanû çûbî, me fehm nekir.
 
How did that happen, I didn't understand.

436
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Mal nehe, axa dehe?
 
Nine houses, ten Aghas?

437
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Nizanim.
 
I don't know.

438
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Avolno me ra şerh kin, em fehm nekir ji xulu.
 
Friends, explain it to us, we didn't understand from the
uncle.

439
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:49,000
Dibê mal nehe, o... axa jî dehe.
 
It says nine houses, and... ten Aghas.

440
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Me fehm nekire, niktê mentiqê gindmira wild e.
 
I didn't understand, the joke of the region of Gindmira
[nearby area] is like that.

441
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:52,000
Niktê ye hewa.
 
That is a joke.

442
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Me'natê gindiz me ra avolno de.
 
Friends, give us the meaning of Gindiz.

443
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Ew oxler in giştik.
 
They are all Aghas [Lords].

444
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Wele, vê gundo ga oxler in a?
 
By God, is this village all Aghas?

445
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:00,000
O, a nêvrim tê kev me ye.
 
Oh, my path falls there too.

446
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,000
Belê reşê...
 
Yes, the dark one...

447
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Oxa nîvro têkewîn.
 
Agha, we entered at noon.

448
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Ser serî û ser çavan, Xwedê xêra te binivîse, Xwedê emrê te
dirêj bike tate.
 
On my head and on my eyes (you are welcome), may God write
down your reward, may God prolong your life, father.

449
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Weleh em xuro no... ez cara ewle me têm vê gundî.
 
By God, we are just... it is the first time I am coming to
this village.

450
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Ez cara ewil têm vê gundê Kurda, Mago, em di virdo nayne?
 
It is the first time I am coming to this Kurdish village,
Mago, do we not come through here?

451
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Xalo tu miletê me, tu silav kî dişîne? Gotina te hene?
 
Uncle, you are our people, who are you sending greetings to?
Do you have any words?

452
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Gelekî gelekî... Xwedê xêra te binivîse.
 
Very, very much... May God write down your reward.

453
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,000
Here...
 
Go...

454
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Hede welehî me ko mirin heke, no ko têkevin gund, xelkê pir
mesxere dikirin, mesele...
 
Come on, by God, we have death [ahead], no, when we enter
the village, people mock a lot, the issue...

455
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Vaye mal nehene, axa dihene...
 
It is that properties don't exist, [but] aghas exist...

456
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Ma mesele ji xelkê naskir, eno gor ez zanim...
 
The issue is known by the people, as far as I know...

457
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Eno gund heft axa kirine axa.
 
That the village has made seven aghas into aghas.

458
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Yanî, yanî ji malekê ge... serek ne, yanî şûre giyo
dimeşiya.
 
Meaning, meaning from one house... they aren't leaders,
meaning the sword of grass was walking [they had fragile
power].

459
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Here...
 
Go...

460
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:55,000
Ka were em têkevine, maşallah. Hewşê jor jî bigire, jor.
 
Come let us enter, Mashallah. Film the upper courtyard too,
up there.

461
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Vê malê jor.
 
That house up there.

462
00:30:57,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Silav li te be, maşallah.
 
Peace be upon you, Mashallah.

463
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Çi gundê heneke...
 
What a cool village...

464
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Xwelî li min ro, gund mekteb di vî gundî da tuneye.
 
Dust on my head [what a shame], there is no school in this
village.

465
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Xwelî li min ro ko mekteb di vî gundî da tuneye, bes barokî
biçûk dînane.
 
What a shame that there is no school in this village, they
have only put a small hut/shelter.

466
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Wek oda biçûk, kobo... vaye ew.
 
Like a small room, man... there it is.

467
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Mekteb di wê de ew dikin.
 
They do the schooling inside that.

468
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Ez bawer dikim qet dikan di vî gundî da tunene.
 
I believe there are no shops at all in this village.

469
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Feqîr çawa dikin di virdo?
 
How do the poor people manage here?

470
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Teb'en miletê vir, gelek ji rê dûr tiştê xwe tînin.
 
Naturally, the people here bring their things from very far
off the road.

471
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:55,000
Mago bi Racû va nêzîk e.
 
They said Mago is near Rajo.

472
00:31:55,000 --> 00:32:01,000
Heft heşt kîlometir hene heta Racû.
 
There are seven or eight kilometers to Rajo.

473
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Malê me re, ono di nav çiya da be, çiqas zor û derd e.
 
Oh our family/people, for it to be in the mountains like
this, what difficulty and trouble it is.

474
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:20,000
We darê behîvê, maşallah te jê behîv ne...
 
That almond tree, Mashallah, have you [picked] almonds from
it...

475
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

476
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Hê behîvên hûrikê din, ê biçinin?
 
There are still small almonds, will they pick them?

477
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Wê ew bikin, xelk dikin, no kin, me dizey dikin, tişto...
 
They will do it, people do it, if not, we will steal,
things...

478
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:45,000
Are weleh.
 
Yes, by God.

479
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Çirnîştek ber vî darî heye.
 
There is a water trough by this tree.

480
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Mago çirnîştek ber vî darî heye.
 
They said there is a water trough by this tree.

481
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Erjêkî curnikî di virdo ye.
 
A trough basin is here.

482
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Mago ev jêkî curnikî... ah, avol no...
 
They said this is a trough... ah, look here...

483
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:02,000
Wadiye?
 
Do you see?

484
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Li vî darî, wekî welkê çêkiribûn, milet hildikişî ser çû
dikir, lê nîn çû pey vaye, wadiye?
 
On this tree, they had made like a shelter, people would
climb up and go do [things], but no, look at it, do you see?

485
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Wekî hêlîn çêkiribûn, çi cî ye.
 
They had made it like a nest, what a place.

486
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:11,000
Ser se ye.
 
It is on the head [excellent].

487
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Ê, bikabê aceb?
 
Eh, will it hold/work I wonder?

488
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Lê bişke?
 
Will it break?

489
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Bûûû...
 
Boo... [Making a sound while looking down or jumping].

490
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Çiqasî hênik e, hênik e bin vî darî.
 
How cool it is, it is cool under this tree.

491
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Darê gûzê ye teb'en, ev darê sîndiyan e.
 
It is a walnut tree naturally, [no] this is an oak tree.

492
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Maşallah...
 
Mashallah...

493
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Havol no.
 
Look here.

494
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Ev darê zeytûnê biner, maşallah.
 
Look at this olive tree, Mashallah.

495
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Koka wê çawa derketiye re.
 
How its root has come out.

496
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Teb'en miletê vî gundî, nexweşê bin vî darî, nexweşê bin vî
darî rûdinin.
 
Naturally the people of this village, the sick under this
tree, the sick sit under this tree.

497
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Bila belayekî dîtibî, tên xwaro virdo dinin.
 
If they have seen a calamity, they come down here and sit.

498
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Wadiye çi caw e? Ha.
 
Do you see what an atmosphere it is? Ha.

499
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Ooo, no ko...
 
Oh, now that...

500
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Çawabû kaba, tew no binvirva xwaro.
 
How it happened man, going down through here.

501
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Eh ya selam... ûx.
 
Oh peace... oof.

502
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Eh.
 
Eh.

503
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Î ro ba vêra, milo were vî darî.
 
Today the wind is here, man come to this tree.

504
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Lenî vî darî, ba yî pak e, bayî tebîî ye.
 
Because at this tree, the air is clean, the air is natural.

505
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Are.
 
Yes.

506
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Î ro ba vêra, vanê... vanê bêjêr da rûniştine go wanh...
vira gundo.
 
Today the wind is here... those... those sitting down below
said that... here is the village.

507
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Rabû wekêra heye, nefesê wekê teng dibe, wan gundo.
 
There is a breeze for you, [if] your breath gets tight,
[come to] the village.

508
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Hîn otisjin, wan vira, bayê xwe pak e, ba pak e.
 
Still oxygen, here, its air is clean, the air is clean.

509
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

510
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Heskirî hest bê.
 
Feel it, let there be feeling.

511
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Ev zeytûnê jî emrê xwe mezin e ha.
 
This olive tree is also old in age, ha.

512
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Wadiye? Çend hemîz ne?
 
Do you see? How many [branches/trunks] are they?

513
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Bes gerek vaden, vaden, gerek vana vaden o.
 
But must [watch out for] wasps, wasps, must [watch out for]
these wasps.

514
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Vaden o, çiçik e, aw bikir, ew nav ro şa kirin, milo mezin
bibo.
 
It is wasps, it is small, does that... they made them happy
inside, man it has grown big.

515
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Ya selam.
 
Oh peace.

516
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Are havol no, xolî mi jî, o cî mosiyo ye o.
 
Yes look here, dust on me too [wow], this is a place of
bees/wasps.

517
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Te mose ne hiştin, gi girtin.
 
You didn't leave bees, they caught/took all.

518
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Girtin he?
 
They caught them?

519
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Lê, mosiye me gi girtin.
 
No, they caught all our bees.

520
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:58,000
Are wela tela herqê xistine, ta wela fetlîniyo.
 
Yes by God, they put [something] in the sweat, by God it
spun.

521
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:59,000
Lê, mose pir bîn.
 
No, there were many bees.

522
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Bes wa dibe, berî me mose girtin.
 
But it seems, they caught the bees before us.

523
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Berî me girtin, maşallah pir tî girtin.
 
They caught them before us, Mashallah they caught a lot.

524
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Lê bî me girtin.
 
What was this?

525
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Lê bî me girtin.
 
No, we caught them.

526
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Are î kî warin, xolûkê wa bibê, mosiyo o.
 
Yes, whoever comes, may it be dust [nothing] for them, it is
[a place of] bees.

527
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,000
Yanî ezîmet cem xolû ne. Xolû a ezîmet no ke, bes heke we
ezîmet cem gindikan.
 
Meaning the invitation is not with the dust [people]. The
dust [people] don't make an invitation, but if the
invitation is with the melons.

528
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Zikê mosekî buade.
 
It gave a bee's stomach.

529
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Ne we?
 
Is it not?

530
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Are selme.
 
Yes, peace.

531
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Xalo tu si silav kî dişînî ji şeva bora milet ra?
 
Uncle, what greetings do you send from the past night to the
people?

532
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:20,000
Dige çi silavê bişînî?
 
Then what greetings will you send?

533
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Tu dibê çi?
 
What do you say?

534
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Em te çawa bikin, çûn zevî?
 
How shall we take you, going to the field?

535
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Weleh ez nizanim, saeto giyo xweş be, ez nizanim.
 
By God I don't know, may the time/grass be good, I don't
know.

536
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Êwa.
 
Yes.

537
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Hola te.
 
Your [greeting/condition].

538
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Aleikum selam.
 
Peace be upon you.

539
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Pencera xwe veke, pencera xwe veke, wano maşallah.
 
Open your window, open your window, like that Mashallah.

540
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Seke.
 
Look.

541
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Çibukî hênik dikişîne mala gundî.
 
What a cool breeze the villager's house draws.

542
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Tadiye? Çi tebîat li hember me ye? Ehê.
 
Do you see? What nature is opposite us? Aha.

543
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:55,000
Wela xolû çi hewş li ser vegirtî.
 
By God [dust], what a courtyard is covered over it.

544
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:57,000
Bino çoq zû cefo di virdo di.
 
Look very quickly the suffering is in here.

545
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Miletê me germ e, cebar e, cebar.
 
Our people are warm, resourceful, resourceful.

546
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:05,000
Mago cebar e, seke hewş ro t'keta girtine, maşallah Xwedê
quwetê bide.
 
They said resourceful, look they have closed the courtyard
[with plants/fences], Mashallah may God give strength.

547
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Li ser vê darê, ana...
 
On this tree, here...

548
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Cî, cî, ana girtî, zane li çi cî girtî.
 
Places, places, here closed, knows in what place it is
closed.

549
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Embar gundek vekirî.
 
A storehouse, an open village.

550
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:34,000
Saeta gunda xweş.
 
The village time is nice.

551
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Me av bo şker, me av bo şker, çûk tê badikin.
 
We broke the water [or filled the water], we broke the
water, the birds are swirling/coming.

552
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Çandinîye çiçik reqa xwe... koşe... çetine.
 
The planting is a bit... its slope... is steep... it is
difficult.

553
00:37:46,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Wadiye?
 
Do you see?

554
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:09,000
Mişkîle şarêa xwe xirab e, ana em têk hatin şarêa erim bo.
 
The problem is its road is bad, here we entered, the road
was destroyed.

555
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:29,000
Çiçik çetine.
 
It is a bit difficult.

556
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Xaltîka ji vî gundî ye?
 
Is the aunt from this village?

557
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Hecî kîme jorê?
 
Hajji, who is the one up there?

558
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:00,000
Ê jor?
 
The one up there?

559
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:01,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

560
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,000
Aaa keça...
 
Uhh, the daughter of...

561
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:04,000
Keçika kê ye?
 
Whose daughter is she?

562
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Keçika wî kî ne?
 
Who is his daughter?

563
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Keçika Egîd e, Egîd.
 
She is Egîd's daughter, Egîd.

564
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Egîd?
 
Egîd?

565
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Tu bavê Egîd nasnakî? Serokê belediyê?
 
Don't you know Egîd's father? The head of the municipality?

566
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Egîd?
 
Egîd?

567
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Ser serê min ser çavê min.
 
Yes, Hajji Egîd.

568
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:11,000
Ser serê min ser çavê min.
 
Upon my head, upon my eyes.

569
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,000
Hecî te ez naskirime?
 
Hajji, did you recognize me?

570
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:14,000
Ez ji mala Husên im.
 
I am from the House of Husên.

571
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:16,000
Haa, mala Se'roş?
 
Ah, the Se'roş family?

572
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,000
Mala Se'roş.
 
The Se'roş family.

573
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:19,000
Ser serê min ser çavê min.
 
Upon my head, upon my eyes.

574
00:41:19,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Rehma Xwedê li dê û bavê te bî.
 
May God have mercy on your parents.

575
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,000
Mehmûd bî?
 
Was it Mahmoud?

576
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:24,000
Cihê meşûr...
 
The famous place...

577
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Lê welle.
 
Oh, really.

578
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,000
...tev hemû xelas bûn.
 
...they are all finished.

579
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Wele.
 
Really.

580
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,000
Hemû reşde 'emê kine (?).
 
All the Rashda are my uncles.

581
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:32,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

582
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:35,000
Tu çima min cenb nekî got te qesta ba?
 
Why don't you stop by me, you said you intended to?

583
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Mala Mela Mistefa...
 
Mullah Mustafa's house...

584
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:38,000
Tu ketîyê ş şûlî?
 
Did you get caught up in work?

585
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:41,000
Tu ketîyê ş şûlî?
 
Did you get caught up in work?

586
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:44,000
Wele maşallah avê vir hênik e.
 
Wow, Mashallah, the water here is cool.

587
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:48,000
Tu çima min cenb nekî got te qesta ba?
 
Why don't you stop by me, you said you intended to?

588
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,000
Wele.
 
Really.

589
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Were xwarê te got te qesta ba?
 
Come down, didn't you say you intended to?

590
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:54,000
Me'nî pênc hezarê min li te hene me bide min.
 
Meaning you owe me five thousand, give it to me.

591
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,000
Wele.
 
Really.

592
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:58,000
Me'nî mîrîk î jalo kuro.
 
It means you are a prince, oh dear boy.

593
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:00,000
Xalo maşallah...
 
Uncle, Mashallah...

594
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:02,000
Xalo Hecî, Hecî kî ne?
 
Uncle Hajji, who is Hajji?

595
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Hecî kî ye navê wî?
 
What is Hajji's name?

596
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:08,000
Mihemed, Mihemed.
 
Mohammed, Mohammed.

597
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Mihemedê Hecî...
 
Mohammed of Hajji...

598
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:12,000
Ser serê min ser çavê min.
 
Upon my head, upon my eyes.

599
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Başe Hecî kî... tu nehatiye Hecîkê?
 
Okay, which Hajji... haven't you come to Hecîk?

600
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Der nexist?
 
Didn't it come out?

601
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:19,000
Bes Hecîkê jêrin, me dar nexistî wele Hecîkê jêrin.
 
Just the lower Hecîk [villagers], we haven't planted trees,
honestly, the lower Hecîk.

602
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:21,000
Çend mal e?
 
How many households is it?

603
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,000
Teqrîben 40 mal e.
 
It is approximately 40 households.

604
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:23,000
40 mal e?
 
40 households?

605
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Teqrîben yani.
 
Approximately, I mean.

606
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:26,000
Hecî, ma we dar nexistî?
 
Hajji, haven't you planted trees?

607
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:28,000
Iiii...
 
Eeee...

608
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:30,000
Der nexistin ne?
 
They didn't plant trees, right?

609
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:32,000
Ê werin, werin Xwedê heye.
 
So come, come, God exists.

610
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:34,000
Înşallah Xwedê emrê we dirêj ke.
 
God willing, may God grant you a long life.

611
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:38,000
Erê, ev gundê jêrî jî, em bûn mêvanê Hecîko ne.
 
Yes, this lower village too, we became guests of the Hecîko
[people].

612
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:41,000
Em gihîştin dawiya vîdyoya xwe, Xwedê ji we gişta razî be.
 
We have reached the end of our video, may God be pleased
with all of you.

613
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:44,000
Erê inşallah bimînin di xweşiyê de, saetên we giha xweş.
 
Yes, God willing, stay in happiness, have a good time.

614
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:47,000
Bimînin di vîdyoyê de, xweş. Bye bye.
 
Stay with the video, [it is] good. Bye bye.

615
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,000
U Omer jî heye.
 
And Omar is here too.

616
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Me çend çepên Omer jî...
 
We [give] a few claps for Omar too...

